tributes to the lives lost on that night  in 2017  have been happening all over the valley  today from downtown las vegas to the new  allegiance stadium  but we begin tonight where the tragedy  began  sasha loftis joining us now live from  the route 91 concert grounds where  survivors and families joined hands  tonight  sasha  denise and brian this was just a  beautiful thing to see today  survivors joined the family and friends  of the fallen  to commemorate them three years since  this dark day  candace bowers  [Music]  the group started with a reading of  names behind the concert grounds  they commemorated each person with a  photo and the ringing of a bell  they then walked to las vegas boulevard  and stood in a group across from  mandalay bay  we saw so many people stare up at that  building with tears in their eyes  we spoke with a few survivors tonight  who say as horrific as it was to go  through this  they're grateful to be a part of this  amazing community  we're really grateful that we can stand  here three years later  and join together and and know that  you know out of a horrible tragedy there  was this  wonderful family that was born and so  we know that wherever we go when we see  the little decals on the cars  or the t-shirts or the hats or whatever  we know that  there's family around  metro police shut down guile street so  the group could hold this memorial  safely there was also a moment where  those here cheered for metro police the  ones that were here  blocking the road and thanked them for  their response on that day three years  ago  there was also as you see behind me a  memorial flowers  things like that to commemorate the  anniversary of the one october shooting  reporting live sasha loftis 8 news now
 

